\title{scMarco: marker gene combinations from binarized single-cell expression}
\description{
scMarco helps choose marker gene combinations (for example split-GAL4
driver pairs) that label a cluster of a single-cell RNA-seq dataset and as
few other clusters as possible. Expression is binarized per cluster with a
mixture model, so a gene is ON, OFF or ambiguous in each cluster and in each
split of the dataset (developmental stage, sex, species, ...).
}
\details{
The package has three parts:
\itemize{
\item an interactive Shiny app, \code{\link[=run_scmarco]{run_scmarco()}}, configured by a YAML file;
\item the combination logic behind the app, usable from R on a dataset loaded
with \code{\link[=ds_load]{ds_load()}} and binarized with \code{\link[=ds_binarize]{ds_binarize()}}: \code{\link[=from_cluster]{from_cluster()}},
\code{\link[=clusters_expressing]{clusters_expressing()}}, \code{\link[=distinct_within]{distinct_within()}}, \code{\link[=pair_offtargets]{pair_offtargets()}},
\code{\link[=find_pairs]{find_pairs()}} and the plots in \code{\link[=onoff_plot]{onoff_plot()}};
\item tools that build and edit datasets in the scMarco h5ad format:
\code{\link[=seurat_to_h5ad]{seurat_to_h5ad()}}, \code{\link[=add_probability]{add_probability()}}, \code{\link[=validate_h5ad]{validate_h5ad()}},
\code{\link[=set_cluster_names]{set_cluster_names()}}, \code{\link[=set_cluster_metadata]{set_cluster_metadata()}} and the legacy
converters \code{\link[=sqlite_to_h5ad]{sqlite_to_h5ad()}} and \code{\link[=h5v1_to_h5ad]{h5v1_to_h5ad()}}.
